ine":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Game Day Kickoff: Appreciating Jeremiah Smith's greatness","description":"What to expect in Week 12, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-19T17:08:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff111926/week-12-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5218778/will-echoles","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will_Echoles"},"pick":{"pick":13,"round":1,"team":"NYJ","via":"DAL","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Will Echoles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Will_Echoles","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-19T05:12:45Z","intro":"William Jamierous Echoles (born August 7, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Ole Miss Rebels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Echoles attended Houston High School in Houston, Mississippi, where he played both defensive and offensive line. As a senior, he was the 4A Mississippi Mr. Football and 4A MHSAA Defensive Player of the Year after recording 59 tackles and seven sacks. Echoles was selected to play in the 2024 All-American Bowl. He committed to the University of Mississippi (Ole Miss) to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Ole Miss in 2024, Echoles appeared in eight games and had nine tackles and 0.5 sacks. He returned to Ole Miss as a starter his sophomore year in 2025."}]}}